AGGREGATION PIPELINES
An Aggregation Pipeline is a framework in MongoDB used to process, transform, filter, group, sort, and analyze documents from a collection.
Think of it like a data processing pipeline:
MongoDB Collection
       ↓
   $match
       ↓
   $group
       ↓
   $sort
       ↓
   $project
       ↓
   Final Result
Each operation is called an Aggregation Stage.
Simple Definition
Aggregation Pipeline = A sequence of stages where the output of one stage becomes the input of the next stage.

