Types of Aggregation Stages
Instead of memorizing every stage individually, you can categorize them based on their purpose.
1. Filtering Stages
Used to remove unwanted documents.
$match

2. Projection / Transformation Stages
Used to select, modify, or create fields.
$project
$set
$addFields
$unset
$replaceWith

3. Grouping Stages
Used to combine documents and calculate values.
$group
$count
Common operators inside $group:
$sum
$avg
$min
$max
$first
$last
$push
$addToSet

4. Sorting and Pagination Stages
$sort
$skip
$limit

5. Array Processing Stages
$unwind
And array operators such as:
$filter
$map
$reduce

6. Join / Relationship Stages
$lookup
$graphLookup

7. Collection Output Stages
Used when aggregation results need to be written somewhere.
$out
$merge

8. Sampling / Statistical Stages
$sample
$bucket
$bucketAuto
These are useful for analytics and data analysis.


